<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:14:00Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Historic gains for Arab-majority parties in Israeli election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:483c40d54e934826c4d48f156af4f1e1f62478995c0dbd966143690c8b9b5008</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T20:32:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/historic-gains-for-arab-majority-parties-in-israeli-election--ef69df2f3ac1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/historic-gains-for-arab-majority-parties-in-israeli-election" /><summary type="html">Two Arab-majority parties are set to win a historic 19 seats in total, amid a record turnout at the polls in Israel on Tuesday. Voters from the community, descendants of Palestinians who stayed after Israel's creation and who make up around 20 percent of the population, have been enraged by the Netanyahu government's ultra-nationalist Jewish vision for the country and the Palestinian territories. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Top US federal judge who handled 9/11, Trump, Maduro cases dies aged 92</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1403ccad54d031c8a95068774fe0329c0f33ca2c7c020a1fd12b77b53720b704</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T20:22:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-top-us-federal-judge-who-handled-9-11-trump-maduro-cases-dies-aged-92--a0e3ae1d91ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-top-us-federal-judge-who-handled-9-11-trump-maduro-cases-dies-aged-92" /><summary type="html">Alvin Hellerstein, a top US judge who was handling the trial against deposed Venezuelan leader Nicholas Maduro and previously oversaw lawsuits stemming from the September 11 attacks on the World Trade Centre and multiple cases involving President Donald Trump, died on Wednesday aged 92.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Bolsonaro's escape to the US: How it happened</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abfeab24e3d6c96129970ec13b63a5100258dc14aafc6edadb9fb7fb78bfdb2e</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T20:06:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-escape-to-the-us-how-it-happened--f71fff4a9188.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-escape-to-the-us-how-it-happened" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro arrived in Florida by private plane Wednesday after fleeing his country in defiance of a court order to surrender his passport. Bolsonaro, who lost a runoff election to incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva on Sunday, is under investigation in Brazil for alleged corruption and money laundering and, with his defeat, is set to lose parliamentary immunity. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Amid uncertainty over EU aid, Vitalii Kim insists Ukraine has no choice but to fight for motherland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd4407ece45c7bdee908e0d9299c99c225ecad64c08d5f464a6d39564e7149b1</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:57:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261028-amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-mot--388c86d76aac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261028-amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-motherland" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Vitalii Kim, Minister for Veterans Affairs of Ukraine. “If Europe will not support us, we also will fight because it's our motherland,” says Kim, insisting that Ukraine's determination to resist Russian aggression will endure regardless of the outcome of negotiations over European financial assistance. Yet behind this assertion of national resolve lies a more complex reality: a country confronting not only the immediate pressures of war, but also its mounting psychological, social and institutional consequences.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Amid uncertainty over EU aid, Vitalii Kim insists Ukraine has no choice but to fight for motherland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efee137e34f6efa957ebcd1c5da69bd428933ee5f219ce46d13508a367a61b87</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:54:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-motherland--f23de8cc008b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-motherland" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Vitalii Kim, Minister for Veterans Affairs of Ukraine. “If Europe will not support us, we also will fight because it's our motherland,” says Kim, insisting that Ukraine's determination to resist Russian aggression will endure regardless of the outcome of negotiations over European financial assistance. Yet behind this assertion of national resolve lies a more complex reality: a country confronting not only the immediate pressures of war, but also its mounting psychological, social and institutional consequences.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bolsonaro flees Brazil for US after election defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcc33a0d1e14b478b1fc5cb3a6a00cb8df424cc04fde688ee92fdfe9b2633947</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:44:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-flees-brazil-for-us-after-election-defeat--be6ab88c3a49.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-flees-brazil-for-us-after-election-defeat" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro's clandestine escape to the United States bewildered Brazil and triggered a frantic search for his whereabouts. The Supreme Court had ordered the son of jailed ex-leader Jair Bolsonaro to forfeit his passports after his electoral loss on Sunday, amid fears he would leave the country due to ongoing investigations against him. But the defeated right-wing presidential candidate failed to hand them in, choosing instead to flee to the US via Argentina and Ecuador. FRANCE 24's Tim Vickery reports from Rio de Janeiro.</summary></entry><entry><title>Which way will Israel break? Netanyahu still in it after election night surprises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ca4c4c1a3282d5455092d324d32d3deeb9f85d94970161524a54780e4caa631</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:34:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261028-which-way-will-israel-break-netanyahu-still-in-it-after-election-night-surprises--5418ddd2326d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261028-which-way-will-israel-break-netanyahu-still-in-it-after-election-night-surprises" /><summary type="html">In Israel, the surprises only start with election night: they're still counting ballots in a vote that featured the highest turnout in decades, historic inroads by Arab parties, Benjamin Netanyahu’s worst result since 1999 and yet Israel’s longest-serving prime minister still has a path to staying in power. As we await the definitive makeup of the next parliament, our panel breaks out the calculators and pie charts: in what scenario does Netanyahu survive? Is the issue with the right-wing Likud leader or his policies?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Spain high-speed train crash kills 68, injures over 100</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b30b53d3ba4b6bd94502d73c7f6316cb8b67cf2dc43d43b094778a01fc978b2</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:32:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-high-speed-train-crash-kills-68-injures-over-100--9e328dc364f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-high-speed-train-crash-kills-68-injures-over-100" /><summary type="html">A high-speed train collision south of Madrid killed 68 people and injured scores more on Wednesday, with the toll likely to rise, authorities said, in one of Europe's deadliest such disasters this century. The second such accident to strike Spain this year will raise fresh questions about the country's rail safety, with the transport minister speaking of an "error" and "inexplicable circumstances" that led to the collision. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Urda, south of Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Israeli electorate has moved rightward: Many underestimated extent of fracture in Israeli society'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91c03a7c703e04c326a15b0e781826dee786b905457fc6482ef3c438128e9995</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:12:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israeli-electorate-has-moved-rightward-many-underestimated-extent-of-fracture-in-israeli-society--c43137dced55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-electorate-has-moved-rightward-many-underestimated-extent-of-fracture-in-israeli-society" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Dr. Shira Efron, RAND's Distinguished Israel Policy Chair. “Many of us, myself included, underestimated the extent of the fracture in Israeli society.” It reflects a political system in which ideological polarisation, the rightward shift of the Jewish electorate and the contested legitimacy of Arab political participation have sharply narrowed the possibilities for coalition-building. Dr. Efron illustrates a political landscape in which Netanyahu’s governing bloc has lost ground, yet still has “more cards, or better cards, to play,” she argues, whether through another election, a national unity government or attempts to draw opposition partners into his orbit.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin woos African leaders as Moscow seeks to expand footprint in Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89d75bb75374a153467ca88d89c89ce9927bb7f534cc3bd69cf1b97272a265c0</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T18:13:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261028-putin-woos-african-leaders-moscow-seeks-expand-footprint-africa--1f573b05cce8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261028-putin-woos-african-leaders-moscow-seeks-expand-footprint-africa" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin sought to woo African leaders and government delegates on Wednesday as they gathered in Moscow for the third Russia-Africa Summit to discuss trade, security, arms deals and grain supplies as part of the Kremlin's strategic efforts to expand its footprint in Africa.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'Si, se puede': US civil rights icon Dolores Huerta dies at 96</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61119273de47568463c59bc880d6a2ea22a33695df2cbf96ad23e6bdbaaefe4a</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T17:49:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-si-se-puede-us-civil-rights-icon-dolores-huerta-dies-96--8714b827ca22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-si-se-puede-us-civil-rights-icon-dolores-huerta-dies-96" /><summary type="html">Influential US labour union co-founder, feminist, and civil rights icon Dolores Huerta died on Wednesday in Bakersfield, California, her family said. Credited with coining the enduring "Si, se puede!" rallying cry later adapted by former US president Barack Obama, Huerta continued her activism on race, poverty, LGBTQ and women's rights issues until the last months of her life.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US grants visa to defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:512fa81e61cffbcaab686dbb690d34b8f8c86d758e4d5a0cec00416f74fa3464</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T17:00:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-us-grants-visa-to-defeated-brazilian-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro--19875dc44dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-us-grants-visa-to-defeated-brazilian-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro and his immediate family landed in Miami, Florida on Wednesday after he refused to surrender his passports as ordered by his country's Supreme Court in connection with a money-laundering probe. The US State Department on Tuesday announced it had granted entry visas to the senator and his family. France 24's Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel election: What impact on Iran as the war in the Middle East continues?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6c814c14f585f697f91af78da6a1184c2d006101631aae2a143c375b678b814</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:54:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israel-election-what-impact-on-iran-as-the-war-in-the-middle-east-continues--3eb40a582df2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israel-election-what-impact-on-iran-as-the-war-in-the-middle-east-continues" /><summary type="html">Benjamin Netanyahu is expected to face greater constraints as Israel’s caretaker prime minister following Tuesday’s election. However, experts say his government could retain significant powers, including the authority to wage war against Iran. So what impact will the election have on Israel’s approach to Iran? France 24’s International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Racist attack in Trappes deeply scars local community</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e627b2787e804d10af382698a98d40f7dea6e10b2ae1e680d0549810352b203</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:53:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-france-racist-attack-in-trappes-deeply-scars-local-community--369e58b75191.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-france-racist-attack-in-trappes-deeply-scars-local-community" /><summary type="html">It has been five days since a gunman opened fire in the Paris suburb of Trappes in a racist attack that left one person dead and five others injured. Over the weekend, hundreds of people marched through the town to pay tribute to the 26-year-old victim, Bossio Wangi, and show solidarity with his family. The attack has left a deep mark on the local community, and mediators have been mobilised to provide support. Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Defeated presidential candidate Bolsonaro lands in Miami after fleeing Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfefd095f36d89a626e35625c0ca67d3a3e7f18714d8828358fd9528620c7139</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:50:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-defeated-presidential-candidate-bolsonaro-lands-in-miami-after-fleeing-brazil--6e4a0f8bfab8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-defeated-presidential-candidate-bolsonaro-lands-in-miami-after-fleeing-brazil" /><summary type="html">Brazilian Senator ​Flavio Bolsonaro and his family arrived in Miami on Wednesday, where the United States government granted them ​entry visas after he refused to comply with a Brazilian Supreme Court order to surrender his passports. Bolsonaro lost Sunday's presidential election to leftist incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia clashes push 50,000 to flee to Kenya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05a5725595e50b4f6fa5eed0814077d81a20f5c5cc53931e95f1fbda346621a4</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:29:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261028-ethiopia-clashes-push-50-000-flee-to-kenya--d0b352552396.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261028-ethiopia-clashes-push-50-000-flee-to-kenya" /><summary type="html">The outbreak of fighting between rival forces in southern Ethiopia last week has led some 50,000 people to seek refuge in neighbouring Kenya, the United Nations said Wednesday, citing local authorities.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: PM Sanchez gives speech on train collision</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb8df1808c6c19e126cecfbc4895af1407d463b81c9b7cfcff554136a975c447</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:29:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-pm-sanchez-gives-speech-on-train-collision--19ea2387e10a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-pm-sanchez-gives-speech-on-train-collision" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez addressed the nation from the site of the train collision in Toledo province, expressing his full solidarity with the victims, their families and all those injured in the tragedy.

Earlier, Transport Minister Óscar Puente said a computer malfunction had disrupted the railway’s safety system. He said the RENFE train had been instructed to resume its journey despite an active stop signal, before crashing into the stationary IRYO train.

The collision on Wednesday killed at least 64 people and injured 58 others. Rescue teams continue to search the wreckage for survivors and bodies.

It is Spain’s second deadly high-speed rail collision this year, following a January crash that killed 46 people.</summary></entry><entry><title>Defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro lands in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b29a7393cde744d9c1ea20657e681defd1beffd47d8248ae9c253ab8e3649ee7</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:28:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-defeated-brazilian-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-miami--1afa0c52e271.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-defeated-brazilian-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-miami" /><summary type="html">Defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro and his family landed in Miami on Wednesday (October 28) after fleeing Brazil. The stunning move came after 48 hours in which Bolsonaro refused to concede to Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and then threatened to attempt to annul the election result. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Tim Vickery.</summary></entry><entry><title>Arab parties ‘have woken up’: Israel's uncertain election may deliver surprise kingmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64adc74157d1cfc0b624c022ac190ec3c614ebe2810a2f553d6f389d0bb84bf7</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:04:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261028-arab-parties-have-woken-up-israel-uncertain-election-may-deliver-surprise-kingmakers--f902aaf3d82e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261028-arab-parties-have-woken-up-israel-uncertain-election-may-deliver-surprise-kingmakers" /><summary type="html">Uncertainty hung over Israel’s election Wednesday as neither Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s right-wing, religious bloc nor the bloc formed by his centrist rival Gadi Eisenkot appeared to be heading for a majority in the Knesset. But there was a surprise: an unusually strong showing by Arab parties could make them unexpected kingmakers.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>John Malkovich and Sam Rockwell head to Chile in new political CIA thriller</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:835ea7c599c9b988b905e238c8efc2f4bfa7ac74b658bb6efded9c783967a3bc</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T15:55:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261028-john-malkovich-and-sam-rockwell-head-to-chile-in-new-political-cia-thriller--d8275ecd7c7a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261028-john-malkovich-and-sam-rockwell-head-to-chile-in-new-political-cia-thriller" /><summary type="html">Four very different films arrive in French cinemas this week, and arts24 critic Emma Jones has seen them all. Martin McDonagh's "Wild Horse Nine" reunites him with an A-list cast. John Malkovich, who won the Volpi Cup for Best Actor at Venice, plays a dying CIA agent in 1973 Chile, alongside Sam Rockwell. Emma calls it her favourite McDonagh film since "In Bruges" and a must see.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Midterms - People Power: Bringing Out the Black Vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9eaeb4ec0234f62d38e5cf08fa0748baacb715259a98696e1359ca5c24180a2</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T15:53:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-2026-midterms-people-power-bringing-out-the-black-vote--85532bffc13d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-2026-midterms-people-power-bringing-out-the-black-vote" /><summary type="html">With the U.S. midterm elections set for November 3, 2026, Scotty Smart is crisscrossing Atlanta, Georgia, to get Black voters to the polls. Facing widespread voter abstention, the activist is determined to turn civic engagement into a force for change.</summary></entry><entry><title>At least 64 dead in Spain’s high-speed train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5274bb73201a7de8184960bf01783f69a616302c2011a6bd13dd4b9218b69267</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T15:37:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-at-least-64-dead-in-spain-s-high-speed-train-crash--c2c0a9282759.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-at-least-64-dead-in-spain-s-high-speed-train-crash" /><summary type="html">At least 64 people died when two Spanish ​high-speed trains collided on Wednesday, with rescue workers scouring the wreckage for more bodies after Spain's second deadly rail accident this year.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli election: Lebanon expects little change in Israeli policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cac0c90fac6f55aaa527b77f1ad0afee6ef06e5586514fcce6f72aaf9911fe45</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:13:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T15:36:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israeli-election-lebanon-expects-little-change-in-israeli-policy--3b56afe2199d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israeli-election-lebanon-expects-little-change-in-israeli-policy" /><summary type="html">The war in the Middle East never really stopped, but Lebanese expect little change in Israeli policy after Israel's elections. In Israel, as votes are counted, no clear winner has emerged yet. France 24's correspondent Renée Davis reports the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Israeli president trying to form unity govt: They will not need Arab parties nor Orthodox parties'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ff3bf99bcabca9e4a251ead2acd39a4e08977ff15f252da2f055b4a052aa6a5</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:14:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T15:11:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israeli-president-trying-to-form-unity-govt-they-will-not-need-arab-parties-nor-orthodox-pa--cb9af04643f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israeli-president-trying-to-form-unity-govt-they-will-not-need-arab-parties-nor-orthodox-parties" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Tamar Sebok, correspondent for the Israeli daily Yedioth Ahronoth, based in France. In an Israeli election marked by political uncertainty, unusually high voter participation and a significant mobilisation of Arab voters, the struggle for power extends far beyond the ballot box. As Sebok explains, the decisive question is not necessarily which party wins the most seats, but which political leader can assemble a viable governing coalition. “You don't know until the coalition is formed who really won,” Sebok explains, capturing the fundamental uncertainty of Israel's parliamentary system. “It's not a question of having the most mandates. It's the question of what kind of acceptance you get from the other parties.”</summary></entry></feed>
